{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqefyksc2io","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Learned model replaces Sonnet judge via shadow-before-enforce rollout","summary":"End goal: a KB-specific learned classifier replaces Sonnet as the primary edge adjudicator (keep/prune verdicts on RAG-retrieved note pairs). Sonnet is the teacher — its verdicts are training data. Rollout phases: (1) Sonnet judges solo, journal rows accumulate as training corpus. (2) Sonnet judges primary; learned model runs in shadow — shadow_verdict + shadow_conf logged on every judge-journal row. (3) Promotion gate: if agreement rate (verdict == shadow_verdict) exceeds threshold (~90-95%) on a rolling held-out window, flip — learned model becomes primary, Sonnet becomes spot-checker. (4) Learned model solo; Sonnet only on low-confidence / OOD cases. Journal schema addition for phase 2: shadow_verdict, shadow_conf, model_version fields on judge-journal rows. The moat is KB-specificity: the learned model captures semantic edge patterns unique to this graph's private notes, which a generic model cannot replicate. Gate-journal is repurposed to shadow metrics only (RAG-only vs DAG-tier agreement); judge-journal is the primary training corpus.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-14T23:54:44.796Z","vec":[-0.062261536717414856,-0.008990964852273464,-0.09786771237850189,-0.03149887174367905,0.044709235429763794,0.0020056685898452997,-0.014114661142230034,-0.014106701128184795,0.017144272103905678,0.0395323820412159,0.03581675514578819,0.032115671783685684,-0.0024416446685791016,0.0020495278295129538,0.00010725391621235758,0.0671459212899208,0.10209856927394867,0.04334678873419762,-0.06589221954345703,0.002614377299323678,-0.011590534821152687,-0.021715812385082245,0.022187672555446625,-0.03704722598195076,-0.027262793853878975,-0.028378760442137718,-0.053280845284461975,0.006779237650334835,0.03435949236154556,-0.16885940730571747,0.005680066533386707,0.059171162545681,-0.02648542635142803